###### Abstract

The Solenoidal Tracker At RHIC (STAR) will search for signatures of a Quark-Gluon Plasma formation. An overview of the capabilities of the STAR detector is presented. The VMB-based Slow Controls system is described. The development of an alternate data acquisition path based on the High-level Data Link Control protocol and the Experimental Physics and Industrial Control System (EPICS) are discussed.

